; An alias or an account block names its target through the
; apply-account stack in force when the directive is read
; (src/textual_directives.cc, instance_t::alias_directive resolving the
; target with top_account()->find_account; account_directive registering
; the block's account under top_account), and register_account expands a
; posting that fired an alias without a second prefix
; (src/journal.cc:169-177).  A `default` account, the account-block form
; of the `bucket` directive, completes the one posting of its
; transaction (src/xact.cc:368, posts.size() == 1, doc/ledger3.texi
; "contain only a single posting"), and an account-block payee maps the
; Unknown account of a matching payee (src/journal.cc:179-188).  The
; semantic bisimulation
; (test/semantic/check_all.py) replays this journal, so an oracle that
; prefixed an alias expansion with the apply stack, or that resolved a
; block account at top level, would fail here.

apply account Top
alias Foo=Foo
alias Food=Bar
account Fee
    alias Fee
account Suspense
    default
account Groceries
    payee Grocer
end apply account
alias Rent=Housing
apply account Home
2024/01/01 X
    Foo    $10
    Food    $5
    Fee    $1
    Rent    $20
    Cash
end apply account
2024/01/02 Solo
    Expenses:Misc    $3
2024/01/03 Grocer
    Unknown    $7
    Assets:Cash

test bal --flat --no-total
                 $-7  Assets:Cash
                  $3  Expenses:Misc
                $-36  Home:Cash
                 $20  Housing
                  $5  Top:Bar
                  $1  Top:Fee
                 $10  Top:Foo
                  $7  Top:Groceries
                 $-3  Top:Suspense
end test
